  "source_scope_disclosure": "Selected original Proposition2.11 linear density phase mixing and scattering under assumed uniform Penrose condition. Retain d>=3, exact M=ceil((d+1)/2), short-range real w, weighted g/Qin hypotheses and exact quantum Sobolev/Fourier-Wigner normalization. Selected N0,N1 are nonnegative integers satisfying N1<N0-d/2-1; this is an explicit restriction of the carrier constants1363 to match the printed integer inverse-Laplace derivative count1339. No nonlinear bootstrap, Coulomb, independently established quantum-to-classical scattering limit or Penrose-sufficiency criterion is selected. Complete source-written Lindhard/Green/resolvent, density convolution, finite-difference and scattering-profile integral core retained.",
