  "difficulty_level": "H3",
  "draft_difficulty_reason": "The assumed Penrose lower bound alone does not provide density decay or a scattering profile uniform as hbar tends to zero. The author supplies the full quantum Lindhard derivative and Green-function inversion estimates, then uses the source-specific free-density convolution to control the interacting density. The complete finite-difference, weighted Fourier-variable and tail-integral argument closes the moving quantum Sobolev scattering estimate with uniform constants, rather than treating that new semiclassical estimate as a standard prerequisite.",
